### Neni 230

Acts with terrorist purposes
(Words removed by law 8733, dated 24.1.2001, amended by law no. 9686, dated 26.2.2007; amended by law no. 23/2012, dated 1.3.2012)

The commission of the following acts, with the purpose of spreading panic among the population or to compel state organs, Albanian or foreign, to perform or not perform a specific act, or to destroy or destabilize, in a serious manner, essential political, constitutional, economic or social structures of the Albanian state, of another state, international institution or organization, is punishable by imprisonment of not less than fifteen years or by life imprisonment.

Acts with terrorist purposes include:
a) acts against the person, which may cause death or serious injury;
b) hijacking of aircraft, ships, other means of transport or fixed platforms or the unlawful exercise of control over them, by force or through the threat of use of force or by means of any other form of threat;
c) commission of acts of violence against a person on board an aircraft in flight, on board a ship or on board a fixed platform, when these acts may endanger the safety of the aircraft, the vessel or the fixed platform;
ç) destruction of an aircraft in operation, a ship or a fixed platform or causing such damage to the aircraft, ship or its cargo or fixed platform, that makes impossible or endangers or may endanger the safety of flight, navigation or the fixed platform;
d) placing, by any means, on an aircraft in service, on a ship or on a fixed platform, a device or substance that may destroy the aircraft, ship or fixed platform or that may cause damage to the aircraft, ship or its cargo or fixed platform and that endangers or may endanger the safety of flight, navigation of the ship or the fixed platform;
dh) destruction or damage of flight equipment or maritime navigation equipment or interference with their operation, when such an act may endanger the safety of the aircraft or ship;
e) dissemination of information known to be false, endangering the safety of an aircraft in flight or a ship in navigation;
ë) killing or kidnapping of an internationally protected person, according to Article 9 of this Code, or any other attack against him or his freedom;
f) violent attack against the office, private residence or means of transport of an internationally protected person, according to Article 9 of this Code, when this attack endangers the person or his freedom;
g) hostage-taking or kidnapping of a person and threatening to kill, to injure or to continue holding him hostage;
gj) taking possession of, possessing, using, transferring, alienating, disposing of or disseminating nuclear material, intentionally and without being legally authorized, when death or serious injury is caused or may be caused to any person or serious damage to property;
h) theft, misappropriation or obtaining through fraud of nuclear materials;
i) demanding nuclear materials, using coercion, violence or any other form of threat;
j) production, possession, purchase, transport or trade of explosive substances, firearms, biological, chemical or nuclear weapons, as well as scientific research for the production of weapons of mass destruction;
k) commission of acts of violence, using any device, substance or weapon, against a person at an international civil aviation airport, when these acts cause or may cause serious injury or death of persons;
l) destruction or serious damage of facilities or equipment at an international civil aviation airport or to an aircraft placed at this airport that is not in flight or interruption of airport services, using any device or weapon, when this act endangers or may endanger the safety of the airport;
ll) dissemination, placement, discharge or detonation of explosive substances or other deadly devices, in public places, in the offices of a state or government, public transport system or in public infrastructure, as well as distribution in the environment of hazardous substances, causing fires, floods, explosions, with the purpose of causing death or serious bodily injury or with the purpose of causing massive destruction of the aforementioned places, facilities or systems, when this destruction brings or may bring major economic losses;
m) serious and large-scale destruction of public property, public infrastructure, transport system, information system and private property, endangering the lives of persons;
n) causing interruption of the supply of water, electricity or any other important resource;

or any other act that aims to cause death or serious injury to civilians or any other person not taking active part in hostilities in a situation of armed conflict, committed for the purposes specified in the first paragraph of this article.
Actions that cause interruption of an important service, a system, a public or private activity, as a result of protest, civil disobedience, or strike, shall not be considered acts with terrorist purposes within the meaning of this article.

### Neni 230/a

Financing of terrorism
(Added by law no. 9086, dated 19.6.2003; amended by law no. 23/2012, dated 1.3.2012; repealed the part providing for punishment by fine, as a principal punishment, alongside imprisonment, by law no. 144, dated 2.5.2013)
The provision or collection of funds, by any means, directly or indirectly, with the intention that they be used or knowing that they will be used, wholly or partially:
a) to commit acts with terrorist purposes;
b) by a terrorist organization;
c) by an individual terrorist;
is punishable by not less than fifteen years imprisonment or by life imprisonment. The provisions of this article apply:
a) to all funds, which include assets of any kind, corporeal or incorporeal, movable or immovable, regardless of the manner of their acquisition, and legal documents or instruments of any kind, also in electronic or digital form, that demonstrate rights or interests over such assets, including bank credits, travellers' checks, bank checks, money orders, shares, securities, bonds, bank guaranteed checks, letters of credit, as well as any other financial instrument, similar to them;
b) regardless of whether the person who commits one of the acts provided for in the first paragraph of this article, is located in the same state or in a different state from that in which the terrorist organization or individual terrorist is located or from the state in which the act with terrorist purposes has been committed or will be committed;
c) in the case provided for by the first paragraph of this article, regardless of whether the funds were actually used to commit the act or acts, for which they were provided or collected, or whether a connection can be established between the funds and one or more concrete acts with terrorist purposes.
Knowledge and intent, according to the first paragraph of this article, are derived from objective factual circumstances.
